From 904a7cd85f9c4e7439180964ffe9b0953358a345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 06:00:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper_Warden: move the blocked-hits breakdown above the
 country table

.stats is repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr)), so a stat card floors at ~150px.
The block split was appended as two 11px .sub lines inside that cell: with
realistic feed-dominated numbers it wrapped to three lines and broke
mid-separator, leaving a dangling pipe at a line end, and the extra height made
that one card taller than the other four.

The card now holds only the number and its label, and the counts render as one
label/value strip above the country table - inside the card whose numbers they
reconcile against. The counting-window note is the last item, pushed to the far
end only when it has something to be pushed away from. Zero buckets stay
suppressed and the strip stays hidden until it has content.

Styled so it cannot read as a continuation of the explanatory text above it:
label style from .toptbl th, value style from .stat .n, on a --panel-2 chip with
the crimson-tinted --line border. Built as DOM nodes with textContent, not
innerHTML - these labels are dict values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
